# ---------------- string parsing ----------------
ESCAPES={'n':'\n','r':'\r','t':'\t','0':'\0','\\':'\\','"':'"',"'":"'",'b':'\b','f':'\f'}
def parse_quoted(text, i):
    """text[i] is quote. Returns (value, end_index_after_quote) or raises ValueError with start."""
    q=text[i]; start=i; i+=1; out=[]
    while i < len(text):
        c=text[i]
        if c=='\\' and i+1 < len(text):
            n=text[i+1]
            if n in ESCAPES:
                out.append(ESCAPES[n]); i+=2; continue
            elif n=='u' and i+2 < len(text) and text[i+2]=='{':
                j=text.find('}', i+3)
                if j!=-1:
                    try:
                        out.append(chr(int(text[i+3:j],16))); i=j+1; continue
                    except Exception: pass
                out.append('\\'); i+=1; continue
            else:
                out.append('\\'); i+=1; continue
        if c==q:
            return ''.join(out), i+1
        out.append(c); i+=1
    raise ValueError(start)

